nd east, were entirely autonomous; others, although administered by court-appointed officials, were only partially controlled from the centre."<br>"The independent provinces still recognised Tang sovereignty and the semi-autonomous ones still accepted appointments made by central government."<br>4. Counties (hsien)"and these in turn into around 1500 countries (hsien) <br>"The really basic form of government, the only level with which the great majority of the population had any contact, was the county under the rule of a magistrate. This was also the lowest level at which the central bureaucracy functioned." <br>5. Districts (hsiang)"while at the bottom were the districts (hsiang), around 16,000 in number. <br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 4265, 'temperature': 0.2})
