(2400-2200 BCE), Psathi (2400-2200 or 2200-1900 BCE) and Mochlos shows that some kind of accounting system existed on Crete since the 2400-2200 BCE period.    Administrative systems, however, were less sophisticated that these adopted in Mainland Greece during the Early Helladic period (2700-2000 BCE).  Administration should be of a relatively low-level and locally relevant nature.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2146, 'temperature': 0.2})
