mbitious local officials who were prepared to accept these unpopular positions..."<br>"During the 1630s the presence of an intendant became the normal rule, where it had previously been sporadic; without an clear intention, the crown was establishing a parallel system of non-venal administrators, with tremendous potential as a tool for centralization." <br>Intendants were about 80 men  who "could rely on the council to issue arrets in line with their recommendations."<br>4. City governorGovernor of Paris <br>5.<br>4. Provincial governor ; Governors 5. Lieutenant-governor <br>5. Prévôt  in a Prévôté<br>6. Leader of a parish<br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2952, 'temperature': 0.2})
