o ten clans, collectively called On-Uighur (i.e. the Ten Uighurs). Of these, the dominant one was the Yaghlakar and, until the second dynasty was founded in 795, the whole empire was ruled by kaghans drawn from the Yaghlakar family." <br>1. Kaghans<br>2. Rulers of the 10 clans?3.4.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2665, 'temperature': 0.2})
2026-06-30 10:51:21,428 [INFO] ('The variable \'Administrative Level\' delineates the complex hierarchical structure of imperial administration around 560 CE, detailing roles from the Emperor to local officials, each with specific functional responsibilities. Considering the detailed descriptions of the *comes sacrarum largitionum* (in charge of taxes and monetary obligations), the *comes rei privatae* (in charge of imperial estates and demesnes), and especially the *Praetorian prefects* (with "unlimited jurisdiction" over all branches of the economy, including supervision of the postal system, public works, urban corporations, and state monopolies), analyze how the division of financial and economic powers within \'<polity>\' between <time-start> and <time-end> might have fostered either synergistic efficiency or significant administrative friction. Your response should identify specific points of potential overlap or conflict, drawing directly from the provided variable description, and be presented as a structured analytical argument, not exceeding 750 words?', None, [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are are history professor writing challenging questions for PhD students.\n\n    Your task is to create a challenging yet well-defined historical exam question based on a variable definition from a historical dataset.\n    Follow the rules below, and return ONLY the final question template, based on the examples provided. \n    \n    1. Begin the question with a concise explanation of the variable's definition, strictly adhering to the provided description, if no description is provided, use the variable name as the basis for the question.\n    2. Ensure all of the following template markers are used:\n        - '<polity>' for polity names (e.g. 'The Papal States')\n        - '<time-start>' and '<time-end>' for temporal scope\n    3. The question should make abundantly clear what the format of the desired response is and that only that response should be given.\n  