heir leader Ekoji Bhonsle (around 1630-84), who, after initial conquests in South India, began to display an interest in developments there. A year later, Ekoji himself became the ruler of Thanjavur and established the Maratha dynasty of the Raja of Thanjavur.    ::2. Karnam  :: “The Nayaks rule in Thanjavur witnessed the introduction of Ayagar system in each village. The officials in this system, the Karnam, Vettiyan, Talayari along with the head of the village called Maniakkaran were entrusted with the prime business of lang collection along with village administration.”  :::3. Vettiyan ::::4. Talayari :::::5. Maniakkaran (village chief)'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2922, 'temperature': 0.2})
